{"step_index":142,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-31T19:40:40Z","content":"**Yes! You literally never have to look at the Blender interface or click a single button.** \n\nBlender has an incredibly scary user interface with thousands of buttons. But because I have the ability to run terminal commands on your computer, we can bypass the UI entirely using something called **Headless Mode** (or Background Mode).\n\nHere is exactly how it would work. You would treat me just like an MCP server:\n\n1.  **You:** You download a free 3D character file (like an `.obj`, `.fbx`, or `.blend` file) and tell me where it is saved on your computer.\n2.  **You:** You type: *\"Make the character wave its hand and render a 3-second video.\"*\n3.  **Me:** I write a complete Python script (`animate.py`) that imports your character, adds lighting, rotates the arm bones to wave, sets up a camera, and tells it to render.\n4.  **Me:** I run a command in your terminal like this: \n    `blender --background --python animate.py`\n5.  **The Result:** Blender runs completely silently in the background. Its interface never even opens on your screen. A few minutes later, an `output.mp4` video file magically appears in your folder.\n\nYou don't have to touch anything inside Blender. The only requirement is that Blender is installed on your Windows machine so I can trigger it from the command line.\n\nIf you have a 3D character file right now and Blender installed, we could literally do this right now. Is that the kind of fully automated workflow you are looking for?","thinking":"**Clarifying User Intent**\n\nI'm trying to decipher the user's request. It seems they want me to perform actions without them needing to interact directly with any complex systems like an MCP. I'm focusing on identifying what they want me to accomplish and how best to achieve that without requiring them to navigate detailed options.\n\n\n**Assessing Blender Automation**\n\nI've been thinking about the Blender automation, and I now believe I can handle it more completely. I realized the AI can write the Python script as expected, and run it via command line or in a background mode. Specifically, the `run_command` tool is capable of launching Blender headlessly on their Windows machine. This entails writing the Python script and executing it with a command like `blender --background --python script.py`. The output video file is the ultimate goal here.\n\n\n"}
